<title>FRANCE: France sees 0.4 percent drop in 97 beet sowings.</title>
<headline>France sees 0.4 percent drop in 97 beet sowings.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French farm ministry, in its first estimate for the 1997 harvest, predicted on Monday that sugar beet sowings may drop by 0.4 percent to 455,000 hectares from 457,000 hectares in 1996.</p>
<p>The ministry said that as of April 1 some 54 percent of area had been sown to sugar beet.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
